      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1885, it was a station on the Central Branch Union Pacific Railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://legendsofkansas.com/wheaton-kansas/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Founded 1881 by German immigrants, Wheaton grew to three newspapers and pioneered telephone poles and gas generators.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://lostkansas.ccrsdigitalprojects.com/wheaton-pottawatomie-county",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Wheaton’s first post office opened July 27, 1870, named Leghorn until 1883, and operated until 1992.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wheaton%2C_Kansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Wheaton is considered an extinct town after its post office closed, yet it remains a small community in Greene Township.",
